Apple is partnering with UK charity The King's Trust to launch a new education program that will help young people build careers in creative industries, Apple <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-the-kings-trust-launch-initiative-to-empower-young-creatives/">said today</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-tim-cook-kings-trust.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1069326" /><br/>
The Apple x King's Trust Creative Labs will give people aged 18 to 30 the opportunity to work with Apple experts as they look into different career paths.<br/>
<br/>
An initial cohort of up to 20 people is participating in specialized workshops to learn "valuable, industry-aligned skills using Apple technologies." The educational experience started this week with music industry and creative workshops timed to the opening of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/22/apple-music-hall-battersea-power-station/">Apple Music Hall</a> at Battersea Power Station in London. Apple chairman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> and King Charles III visited <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> Hall to meet with attendees.<br/>
<br/>
More cohorts and more sessions will follow over the next year.<br/>
<br/>
